---
title: ROOT KEYS
--- 
%% Made in Mermaid (https://mermaid.live)
%% DESCRIPTION: This diagram shows how all the root keys are computed and stored. The lower-hierarchy keys and data are not shown here - they have separate diagrams.
%% DIAGRAM SUMMARY: A password-derived key (KEK) is used to decrypt 2 root keys: Root DEK (Data Encryption Key) and Root IK (Identity Key). Encrypted and authenthicated data/keys are stored on the server

%% SHAPES:
%% - Rectangles mean operations/algorithms
%% - Rounded rectangles mean data
%% - Dashed borders mean that the diagram ends there, but the logic does not and more detailed info can be found elsewhere
%% - Parallelograms mean user input
%% COLORS:
%% - Red means the most-confidential secrets that are never stored persistently in plaintexts, and should only be computed by the client when really needed (which isn't needed often). A compromise means that the account cannot be secured anymore and should be completely deleted and re-created.
%% - Orange means secrets that still allow access to the account's private data, however, security of the FUTURE data can still be restored by choosing new keys if the current ones leak (assuming nothing "red" was leaked). "Orange" secrets might need to be stored persistently to allow access.

flowchart TB
    classDef red color:#f00,stroke:#f00
    classDef orange color:#f60,stroke:#f60
    classDef dashed stroke-dasharray: 5 5

    subgraph SERVER
        %% SERVER STORAGE
        wrappedDek(["Wrapped Data Encryption Key (DEK)"])
        wrappedRootIKPriv(["Wrapped Root Identity Key (Root IK) priv"])
        userAccount([Non-secret user account data])
        encUserData(["Other encrypted user data, including more wrapped keys (details in other docs)"])
        class encUserData dashed
    end

    subgraph CLIENT
        %% PASSWORD KEY DERIVIATION
        login[/"User login (from UI or from server if user logged in via email/phone)"/] -->|salt| passHash["`Hash function (argon2id)`"]
        pass[/USER PASSWORD/] -->|payload| passHash
        passHash --> kek(["Key encryption key (KEK)"])
        class pass,kek red

        %% ROOT DEK
        kek -->|key| rootDekAead["Symmetric encryption + auth (AEAD)"]
        rootDekAead --> rootDek(["Root Data Encryption Key (Root DEK)"])
        rootDek -->|key| dataKeysAead["AEAD"]
        dataKeysAead --> plainDataKeys(["Unwrapped private keys and data encryption keys (details in other docs)"])
        plainDataKeys --> dataKeysEnd@{ shape: text, label: "....." }
        class rootDek,plainDataKeys orange
        class plainDataKeys dashed

        %% IDENTITY KEYS
        kek -->|key| rootIkPrivAead["Symmetric encryption + auth (AEAD)"]
        rootIkPrivAead --> rootIkPriv(["Root Identity Key (Root IK) priv"])
        class rootIkPriv red
        rootIkPriv -->|private key| rootIkSignature["Signatures of Operational Identity Keys (further info in Identity Keys docs)"]
        class rootIkSignature dashed
        rootIkSignature --> rootIkEnd@{ shape: text, label: "....." }
    end

    %% SERVER-CLIENT TRANSFERS
    wrappedDek -->|payload| rootDekAead
    wrappedRootIKPriv -->|payload| rootIkPrivAead
    userAccount -->|login| login
    encUserData -->|payload| dataKeysAead
